1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,500
MAN: Sandra - I seem to remember you had some family visitors staying with you recently.

2
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:07,640
SANDRA: Yeah that's right. My brother

3
00:00:07,640 --> 00:00:10,190
and his family were here a couple of months ago.

4
00:00:10,190 --> 00:00:15,307
MAN: OK good. Well I wanted to ask your advice - I've got my cousin

5
00:00:15,307 --> 00:00:17,920
and her family visiting next month

6
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:22,470
and as I don't have kids I've no idea where to take them.

7
00:00:22,470 --> 00:00:27,030
SANDRA: Right. What about accommodation? Are they going to stay with you in your flat?

8
00:00:27,030 --> 00:00:29,400
MAN: No, thankfully - there wouldn't be room

9
00:00:29,980 --> 00:00:34,130
my cousin wants me to recommend a hotel. Do you know anywhere?

10
00:00:34,130 --> 00:00:39,410
SANDRA: Yes, I do actually. I always recommend people stay at the Kings Hotel.

11
00:00:39,410 --> 00:00:40,780
MAN: Where's that near?

12
00:00:40,780 --> 00:00:45,316
SANDRA: It's about five minutes' walk from Murray Station - so nice and central.

13
00:00:45,316 --> 00:00:47,260
It's actually on George Street.

14
00:00:47,260 --> 00:00:51,860
MAN: Oh yes I know. I think they're on quite a tight budget

15
00:00:52,060 --> 00:00:55,240
so how much roughly is it to stay there?

16
00:00:55,240 --> 00:00:59,885
SANDRA: If you book a family room it's about £125 per night.

17
00:00:59,885 --> 00:01:03,040
My brother paid for two double rooms in the end

18
00:01:03,100 --> 00:01:07,030
and I think that was around £95 for each room.

19
00:01:07,030 --> 00:01:08,510
MAN: Oh that's not too bad.

20
00:01:08,510 --> 00:01:11,160
SANDRA: So how old are your cousin's kids?

21
00:01:11,160 --> 00:01:16,260
MAN: Twelve and nine. So I want to organise some trips while they're here.

22
00:01:16,260 --> 00:01:19,800
MAN: I was thinking of doing a bus tour of the city centre

23
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:22,650
as none of them have been here before.

24
00:01:22,650 --> 00:01:24,794
SANDRA: Those bus tours are quite expensive.

25
00:01:24,794 --> 00:01:27,820
I think it's better to do a walking tour

26
00:01:28,140 --> 00:01:30,920
it gives you a much better feel for the city.

27
00:01:30,920 --> 00:01:32,980
SANDRA: There's one that starts from Carlton Square

28
00:01:33,520 --> 00:01:36,290
It takes a couple of hours and doesn't cost that much.

29
00:01:36,290 --> 00:01:38,940
MAN: Sounds good. I'll look that up - thanks.

30
00:01:38,940 --> 00:01:43,183
SANDRA: If the weather's nice, one thing you could do is visit the old fort.

31
00:01:43,183 --> 00:01:46,630
You can get there by boat. The whole trip takes half a day.

32
00:01:46,630 --> 00:01:50,740
MAN: That's a really good idea. I'd like to do that myself.

33
00:01:50,740 --> 00:01:55,725
MAN: And if the weather's bad I was thinking they could go to the Science Museum.

34
00:01:55,725 --> 00:01:58,950
But maybe they could do that when I'm at work.

35
00:01:58,950 --> 00:02:02,150
SANDRA: Yeah - don't forget it's closed on Mondays.

36
00:02:02,150 --> 00:02:07,650
MAN: They're here from Saturday for four nights - so Tuesday would be best, I think.

37
00:02:07,650 --> 00:02:11,690
SANDRA: Mmm, and it won't be so crowded then. Saturdays are terrible.

38
00:02:11,690 --> 00:02:14,680
SANDRA: I took my kids to the exhibition on old computers there

39
00:02:14,680 --> 00:02:16,241
and it was far too crowded.

40
00:02:16,241 --> 00:02:18,770
I wanted to go back but it's finished now.

41
00:02:18,770 --> 00:02:22,810
MAN: That's a shame. My cousin's kids would have enjoyed that.

42
00:02:22,810 --> 00:02:26,990
SANDRA: There's another one starting soon on space which looks really good too.

43
00:02:26,990 --> 00:02:30,520
MAN: OK, well I'll mention that to my cousin.

44
00:02:30,520 --> 00:02:33,600
SANDRA: Have you thought about where to take them to eat?

45
00:02:33,600 --> 00:02:37,532
MAN: Well I really like all the food stalls at Clacton Market.

46
00:02:37,532 --> 00:02:43,430
My cousin's vegetarian - I know it's one of the best places for that kind of food.

47
00:02:43,430 --> 00:02:47,370
SANDRA: Definitely, and there'll be loads of choice for the kids, too.

48
00:02:47,370 --> 00:02:49,812
SANDRA: You need to get there quite early though -

49
00:02:49,812 --> 00:02:53,340
at the weekend most of the stalls stop serving lunch at 2.30.

50
00:02:53,340 --> 00:02:56,929
MAN: Good point. It's all going to need careful planning!

51
00:02:56,929 --> 00:03:01,380
My cousin said she'd love to take the kids to a show at the theatre

52
00:03:01,620 --> 00:03:03,780
but tickets are so expensive!

53
00:03:03,780 --> 00:03:06,420
SANDRA: I know. But you can get some good deals

54
00:03:06,420 --> 00:03:09,441
if you book online with bargaintickets.

55
00:03:09,441 --> 00:03:14,040
com for the following day - on some seats there's a 75% discount.

56
00:03:14,040 --> 00:03:16,920
MAN: Really?! I must try and get some.

57
00:03:16,920 --> 00:03:20,200
SANDRA: Yeah. There are lots of things you can do for free as well

58
00:03:20,580 --> 00:03:22,110
no need to spend a fortune.

59
00:03:22,110 --> 00:03:23,290
MAN: Like what?

60
00:03:23,290 --> 00:03:25,617
SANDRA: They're coming next month, right?

61
00:03:25,617 --> 00:03:31,600
Well, check and see if it's the same weekend as the Roots Music Festival in Blakewell Gardens.

62
00:03:31,600 --> 00:03:34,530
MAN: R double-O-T-S?

63
00:03:34,530 --> 00:03:36,040
SANDRA: Yeah. Check it out online

64
00:03:36,560 --> 00:03:40,030
It's always a family-friendly event and there's no entry charge.

65
00:03:40,030 --> 00:03:41,490
MAN: That sounds perfect.

66
00:03:41,490 --> 00:03:44,780
SANDRA: And if you're in Blakewell Gardens - climb Telegraph Hill -

67
00:03:44,780 --> 00:03:47,700
you'll be able to look right down on the port

68
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:51,060
Everyone's always really impressed because it's so huge.

69
00:03:51,060 --> 00:03:56,570
MAN: Oh yeah - I've been meaning to do that for ages. I've heard the view's amazing.

70
00:03:56,570 --> 00:03:58,740
SANDRA: Yeah. It's really worth the effort.

71
00:03:58,740 --> 00:04:04,840
MAN: Well that's given me loads of ideas. Thanks so much...
